WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:03.024
China is building the
biggest dam project on Earth,

00:00:03.354 --> 00:00:05.784
right above one of
India's mightiest rivers.

00:00:05.954 --> 00:00:08.804
The river starts in Tibet
as the Yarlung Tsangpo.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:13.500
It enters Arunachal as the Siang,
becomes the Brahmaputra in Assam,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.200
then flows on into Bangladesh.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:20.430
China's planned hydropower project near
the Great Bend is reported to be around

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.120
60,000 megawatts,
far bigger than the Three Gorges Dam.

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:24.941
Here's the catch:

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:28.671
most of the Brahmaputra's monsoon
water is added inside India,

00:00:28.671 --> 00:00:30.721
by rain and tributaries.

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:32.461
A dam can't switch the river off.

00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:35.287
But it can change when and
how much water arrives.

00:00:35.462 --> 00:00:38.012
Part 2 tomorrow: what happens to Assam.

00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:39.342
Should India be worried?

00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:40.333
Comment below.

